# Feature name: consecutive_rank_diff_mean
# Feature description: Mean of differences between consecutive card ranks (V2, V4, V6, V8, V10) to capture sequential patterns indicating the possibility of straights or other ordering patterns.
# Usefulness: This helps identify if the hand has cards ranked sequentially (important for identifying Straights, Straight Flush, Royal Flush). Sequential rankings are a key attribute of these poker hands.

df['consecutive_rank_diff_mean'] = (df['V4'] - df['V2'] + df['V6'] - df['V4'] + df['V8'] - df['V6'] + df['V10'] - df['V8']) / 4
end

